Author: Jeffrey Cutter <jeff_m_cutter@...109...>

Update contrib/pull-resolv-conf/client.up for no DOMAIN

When no DOMAIN is received from push/pull, do not add either domain or sear=
ch to the resolv.conf.
Fix typo in comment resolv.con[f].
Only add new line when using domain or search.

Signed-off-by: Jeffrey Cutter <jeff_m_cutter@...109...>
---=C2=A0contrib/pull-resolv-conf/client.up | 13 ++++++++-----=C2=A01 file =
changed, 8 insertions(+), 5 deletions(-)
diff --git a/contrib/pull-resolv-conf/client.up b/contrib/pull-resolv-conf/=
client.upindex b28d4d1..8858b47 100644--- a/contrib/pull-resolv-conf/client=
.up+++ b/contrib/pull-resolv-conf/client.up@@ -50,9 +50,10 @@ nl=3D'=C2=A0#=
 or=C2=A0# "dhcp-option DNS 10.10.10.10" (multiple allowed)
-# each DNS option becomes a "nameserver" option in resolv.con+# each DNS o=
ption becomes a "nameserver" option in resolv.conf=C2=A0# if we get one DOM=
AIN, that becomes "domain" in resolv.conf=C2=A0# if we get multiple DOMAINS=
, those become "search" lines in resolv.conf+# if we get no DOMAINS, then d=
on't use either domain or search.
=C2=A0while true; do=C2=A0 =C2=A0eval fopt=3D\$foreign_option_${i}@@ -78,13=
 +79,15 @@ while true; do=C2=A0 =C2=A0i=3D$((i + 1))=C2=A0done
-ds=3Ddomain-if [ $ndoms -gt 1 ]; then- =C2=A0ds=3Dsearch+ds=3D""+if [ $ndo=
ms -eq 1 ]; then+ =C2=A0ds=3D"${nl}domain"+elif [ $ndoms -gt 1 ]; then+ =C2=
=A0ds=3D"${nl}search"=C2=A0fi
=C2=A0# This is the complete file - "$domains" has a leading space already-=
out=3D"# resolv.conf autogenerated by ${0} (${1})${nl}${dns}${nl}${ds}${dom=
ains}"+out=3D"# resolv.conf autogenerated by ${0} (${1})${nl}${dns}${ds}${d=
omains}"
=C2=A0# use resolvconf if it's available=C2=A0if type resolvconf >/dev/null=
 2>&1; then--2.4.3
=20=20=

